    {
      "id": "claim_3d917a6909904bd3a1fe84452efd8fa7",
      "statement": "The L5 chain is tamper-evident, not tamper-proof: a rewrite by the directory operator is detectable only by parties who fetched a signed checkpoint (or retained an earlier head or mirror copy) before the rewrite, and omission of events is not detectable by any mirroring; OPERATE.md therefore instructs consumers who care to poll /v1/audit/head and later run a mirror, and SPEC instructs mirror operators to download the full chain periodically and compare heads against the operator's out-of-band checkpoint publication.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/OPERATE.md#L74-L82",
