    {
      "id": "claim_635f6eda3d574278a9093086c82d52de",
      "statement": "Because a hostile directory operator can lie about listings but cannot sign as an agent, consumers must re-verify an agent's own /.well-known/haap.json against the fingerprint shown in a listing before trusting it — endpoint_proof_at (trust row M3) proves control only at registration time, not ongoing control — and high-stakes consumers use the directory_fingerprint carried on every response (row M12) to cross-check multiple directories, since directories may differ under federation.",
