    {
      "id": "claim_78b86b44c9374d8b9b8927c58291f5ab",
      "statement": "ingest_chain fetches the served head only after paging the whole log, so its matches_served_head reflects a point-in-time snapshot: on a live directory an entry appended between the last log page and the head fetch yields matches_served_head False without any tampering, so an operator treats a mismatch as a retry, and durable rewrite-detection requires re-running the mirror on a cadence while retaining earlier verified heads and checkpoints for later comparison.",
